# quest.assumptions — established whole-program facts, with provenance.
#
# Facts the transformer may RELY ON, so a future solver does not re-derive them
# per routine.  Each row states the claim, the evidence, and what would
# FALSIFY it.  Checked by compiler/check_assumptions.py, which is wired into
# tests/run_lowerc_difftest.sh; a row nobody checks is a row that quietly stops
# being true.
#
# Seeded by Project 53 (docs/Project53/PROMPT.md) with the one established
# fact: the three static pointer words whose bit 31 is clear.  That upgrades
# IR.md §5.10.8's census from "1,008 provable, 27 assumed" to provable
# everywhere — the dereference rewrite M32[M32[a]] -> M32[R[a]] has its
# precondition at every site in the program.
#
# WHY IT HOLDS, and it is NOT "the game stores a small number there":
# each address has exactly ONE direct writer, that writer is Eagle STARTUP
# code, and for two of the three the value is written by the OS through a
# by-reference argument to ?GET_SHARED_PAGE, which returns a mapped page
# address.  A mapped page address in this process has bit 31 clear.
#
# P53 CORRECTION to the prompt's seed text: "sole writer" is true of DIRECT
# stores only.  0x70000210 and 0x70000212 are ALSO passed BY REFERENCE as
# argument 2 of ?GET_SHARED_PAGE, so the OS writes them after the game's own
# store — which is the reason for the assumption, not a hole in it.  A checker
# that counted only LWSTA sites would be checking the wrong thing while looking
# right.  Hence each row carries BOTH halves.
#
# format: <claim> <address> <direct-writer-pc> <address-taken-pc|-> <callee|->
#
ptr-bit31-clear 0x70000210 7015be48 7015bed9 ?GET_SHARED_PAGE
#   SD_PTR.  Direct store `LWSTA 0,[0x70000210]` @7015be48 (startup).  Its
#   ADDRESS is pushed @7015bed9 as argument 2 of ?GET_SHARED_PAGE @7015bedf,
#   which writes the mapped page address through it.
#   FALSIFIED BY: a second direct writer; a second address-taken site; any
#   translated routine assigning SD_PTR.
ptr-bit31-clear 0x70000212 7015bee6 7015bef4 ?GET_SHARED_PAGE
#   OBJ_PTR.  Direct store @7015bee6 of `LLEF 0,[0x70017C00]` — a CONSTANT
#   effective address, so the game-side value is provable by inspection, not
#   assumed.  The assumption covers only what ?GET_SHARED_PAGE @7015befa
#   writes over it through the address pushed @7015bef4.
#   FALSIFIED BY: as above, for OBJ_PTR.
ptr-bit31-clear 0x700007A0 7015c2d6 - -
#   A cached PLAYER element pointer.  Sole writer @7015c2d6, and NO site takes
#   its address, so no runtime routine can write it.  Computed as
#   SD_PTR + 686*n - 642: `WMUL 1,0` (686 = PLAYER's stride), `LWADD
#   0,[0x70000210]`, `XLEF 2,[ac2+0x7D7E]` (-642 on the 15-bit field, which is
#   declarations.json's own "min K seen -642" for that table).  So it is
#   ARITHMETIC ON 0x70000210 and inherits its bit-31 property; it is not an
#   independent assumption.
#   FALSIFIED BY: a second direct writer; any site taking its address; any
#   translated routine assigning it.
